summary: D227's orderings between two CPU contexts, a process and its copy over a shared page, as each backend lowers them (D499): a message passed through a release store and an acquire load carries the ordinary write before it, and two seq_cst stores each followed by a seq_cst load of the other's location never both read the old values, in rounds whose starts are staggered; it cannot show that a weaker outcome would occur without the orderings, only that none the orderings forbid was seen
